================================================================================
Data

Values derived from the following data sets are committed as constants or reduced tables with
their citations; the data sets themselves are not committed (plan R05, R05.T12.d, ruled
2026-10-02; plan R08, ruled 2026-10-09).

- Solar spectral irradiance values derived from ASTM E490-00a(2019), obtained from the U.S. DOE
  National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR, formerly NREL); credit DOE/NLR/Alliance. In
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/solar.ts.

- CIE 2019, Colour-matching functions of CIE 1931 standard colorimetric observer, International
  Commission on Illumination (CIE), Vienna, AT, DOI: 10.25039/CIE.DS.xvudnb9b, licensed under
  CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The values in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/solar.ts are computed from it, integrated against
  E-490; to the extent they are adapted material they are offered under CC BY-SA 4.0.

- Ozone absorption cross-sections at 233 K: Serdyuchenko et al., Atmos. Meas. Tech. 7 (2014) 625;
  Gorshelev et al., Atmos. Meas. Tech. 7 (2014) 609 (IUP Bremen), as binned by Bruneton 2017. In
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/earth.ts; binned to 1 nm in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/absorbers/crossSections.json.

- Methane absorption cross-sections at 100, 198 and 296 K: E. Karkoschka and M. G. Tomasko,
  "Methane absorption coefficients for the jovian planets from laboratory, Huygens, and HST
  data", Icarus 205 (2010) 674-694, DOI: 10.1016/j.icarus.2009.07.044, as converted to
  cross-sections by NASA's Planetary Spectrum Generator (G. L. Villanueva et al., J. Quant.
  Spectrosc. Radiat. Transfer 217 (2018) 86-104; https://psg.gsfc.nasa.gov, file
  data/linelists/xuv/data/ch4.txt, fetched 2026-10-09). Resampled values in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/absorbers/crossSections.json.

- Refractive indices of 75 and 84.5 wt% sulphuric acid at 300 K: K. F. Palmer and D. Williams,
  "Optical constants of sulfuric acid; application to the clouds of Venus?", Appl. Opt. 14
  (1975) 208-219, DOI: 10.1364/AO.14.000208, as distributed by the Aerosol Refractive Index
  Archive (ARIA), University of Oxford, https://eodg.atm.ox.ac.uk/ARIA/. Reduced to the visible
  in apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/sulphuric-acid-75.json and
  sulphuric-acid-84.json.

- Refractive indices of Martian dust: M. J. Wolff et al., "Wavelength dependence of dust
  aerosol single scattering albedo as observed by the Compact Reconnaissance Imaging
  Spectrometer", J. Geophys. Res. 114 (2009) E00D04, DOI: 10.1029/2009JE003350, as
  distributed by NASA Ames's Mars Climate Modeling Group (Dust_Refractive_Indicies.txt) and
  kept in S. Ranjan's ranjanwordsworthsasselov2017b repository (commit 1e67a481). Reduced to the
  visible in apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/mars-dust.json.

- Refractive indices of Titan tholin: B. N. Khare et al., "Optical constants of organic tholins
  produced in a simulated Titanian atmosphere: From soft x-ray to microwave frequencies",
  Icarus 60 (1984) 127-137, DOI: 10.1016/0019-1035(84)90142-8, as distributed in the HITRAN2024
  aerosol compilation (I. E. Gordon et al., J. Quant. Spectrosc. Radiat. Transfer 353 (2026)
  109807; https://hitran.org/aerosols/). Reduced to the visible in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/tholin.json.

- Refractive indices of amorphous Mg2SiO4: C. Jaeger, J. Dorschner, H. Mutschke, Th. Posch and
  Th. Henning, "Steps toward interstellar silicate mineralogy. VII. Spectral properties and
  crystallization behaviour of magnesium silicates produced by the sol-gel method", Astron.
  Astrophys. 408 (2003) 193-204, DOI: 10.1051/0004-6361:20030916, as distributed in the
  HITRAN2024 aerosol compilation (as above). Reduced to the visible in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/forsterite-amorphous.json.

- Refractive indices of ammonia ice and of amorphous MgSiO3: J. V. Martonchik, G. S. Orton and
  J. F. Appleby, "Optical properties of NH3 ice from the far infrared to the near ultraviolet",
  Appl. Opt. 23 (1984) 541-547, DOI: 10.1364/AO.23.000541; J. Dorschner, B. Begemann,
  Th. Henning, C. Jaeger and H. Mutschke, "Steps toward interstellar silicate mineralogy. II.
  Study of Mg-Fe-silicate glasses of variable composition", Astron. Astrophys. 300 (1995)
  503-520; as distributed in optool's lnk_data (C. Dominik, M. Min and R. Tazaki, ascl:2104.010;
  https://github.com/cdominik/optool, commit 0b1fa6df). Reduced to the visible in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/ammonia-ice.json and
  enstatite-glass.json.

- Refractive indices of liquid water, water ice, liquid and solid methane, iron and soot, from
  the refractiveindex.info database (M. N. Polyanskiy, Sci. Data 11, 94 (2024); commit c5c2f188),
  which is dedicated to the public domain (CC0 1.0): G. M. Hale and M. R. Querry, Appl. Opt. 12
  (1973) 555-563, DOI: 10.1364/AO.12.000555; S. G. Warren and R. E. Brandt, J. Geophys. Res. 113
  (2008) D14220, DOI: 10.1029/2007JD009744; J. V. Martonchik and G. S. Orton, Appl. Opt. 33
  (1994) 8306-8317, DOI: 10.1364/AO.33.008306; P. B. Johnson and R. W. Christy, Phys. Rev. B 9
  (1974) 5056-5070, DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevB.9.5056; W. H. Dalzell and A. F. Sarofim, J. Heat
  Transfer 91 (1969) 100-104, DOI: 10.1115/1.3580063. Reduced to the visible in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/water.json, water-ice.json,
  methane-liquid.json, methane-ice.json, iron.json and soot.json.

- The refractive index of CO2 ice: a two-term Cauchy fit to S. G. Warren, "Optical constants of
  carbon dioxide ice", Appl. Opt. 25 (1986) 2650-2674, DOI: 10.1364/AO.25.002650, Table I, with
  the imaginary index from G. B. Hansen, "Ultraviolet to near-infrared absorption spectrum of
  carbon dioxide ice from 0.174 to 1.8 um", J. Geophys. Res. 110 (2005) E11003,
  DOI: 10.1029/2005JE002531. Derived values in
  apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/materials/carbon-dioxide-ice.json.

