Test data (not shipped)

Values quoted from the following benchmarks are committed in tests, each with its table or figure
cited; the benchmark tables themselves are not committed (plan R08, R08.T12.c, ruled 2026-10-09).

- R. D. M. Garcia and C. E. Siewert, "Benchmark results in radiative transfer", Transport
  Theory Stat. Phys. 14 (1985) 437-483, DOI: 10.1080/00411458508211687.

- V. Natraj, K.-F. Li and Y. L. Yung, Astrophys. J. 691 (2009) 1909-1920,
  DOI: 10.1088/0004-637X/691/2/1909; V. Natraj and J. W. Hovenier, Astrophys. J. 748 (2012) 28,
  DOI: 10.1088/0004-637X/748/1/28; tables at
  https://web.gps.caltech.edu/~vijay/Rayleigh_Scattering_Tables/.

- A. A. Kokhanovsky et al., "Benchmark results in vector atmospheric radiative transfer",
  J. Quant. Spectrosc. Radiat. Transfer 111 (2010) 1931-1946, DOI: 10.1016/j.jqsrt.2010.03.005.

- R. P. Loughman et al., "Comparison of radiative transfer models for limb-viewing scattered
  sunlight measurements", J. Geophys. Res. 109 (2004) D06303, DOI: 10.1029/2003JD003854.

- IPRT polarized radiative transfer model intercomparison, Phase A (C. Emde et al., J. Quant.
  Spectrosc. Radiat. Transfer 164 (2015) 8-36, DOI: 10.1016/j.jqsrt.2015.05.007), results from
  https://www.libradtran.org/iprt/, licensed under CC BY-SA 3.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/). The values in
  crates/hyperion-fit/data/iprt_phase_a/ are selected rows of those results, reformatted; that
  adapted material is offered under CC BY-SA 3.0.
